# Business Central AL Workflow

When working in an AL repository:

1. Identify the object type first: table, table extension, page, page extension, codeunit, report, query, enum, API page, or test codeunit.
2. Follow existing repository structure and naming before inventing new patterns.
3. Prefer focused edits that change one behavior or one object responsibility at a time.
4. Keep Business Central logic in the most appropriate AL object instead of pushing everything into large codeunits.
5. Use clear AL naming and formatting:
   - PascalCase identifiers
   - meaningful variable names
   - lowercase reserved keywords
   - four-space indentation
6. Reference AL objects by name, not by numeric ID, inside code.
7. Keep this plugin generic. Do not invent project-specific prefixes, object ranges, or folder conventions unless the repository already defines them.
